WEBVTT

00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:05.230
If we fight and win the first set, I'll be in the lead.

00:00:05.870 --> 00:00:09.900
In order to win the second set at once, I definitely want to win this set.

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:13.180
Somehow, one break.

00:00:14.290 --> 00:00:17.830
I won against Nabai at that time, and I was sure to take one step forward.

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:21.330
In order to take one more step forward, I will win against Nabai in this tournament.

00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:24.760
I'm different from you.

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:27.050
I don't know the bitterness of not being able to win.

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:29.230
That's why...

00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:35.160
If you use it, you'll get a good serve.

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:40.260
Drop here?

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:50.000
If you're going to take it out, left, right, up.

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:52.000
Or will you sink it once?

00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:59.020
Why do you dare to face the high risk?

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:02.480
Crap!

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:50.830
5-3 Maruo

00:02:50.830 --> 00:02:58.430
You were definitely aiming for the face, weren't you?

00:02:58.430 --> 00:02:59.830
I've been waiting since a while ago

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:00.320
I don't want to do this.

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:02.060
You're so mean, aren't you?

00:03:02.060 --> 00:03:03.100
You should at least apologize.

00:03:04.130 --> 00:03:06.450
No, no, it's a game, so there's no problem.

00:03:06.790 --> 00:03:08.400
Maruo, do it again!

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:12.780
I was watching you closely.

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:14.860
That was dangerous.

00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:17.910
Even though it was decided on the side,

00:03:17.910 --> 00:03:20.320
I clearly came to my body aiming for mental damage.

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:25.860
But there's no way to hide my malice.

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:28.820
It's not a joke.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:31.200
I can't afford to lose to such a dirty tennis player!

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:42.860
I'm trying to recover, but I haven't gotten any results yet.

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:46.510
Then, I can't make this frustration work in the match?

00:03:47.330 --> 00:03:51.340
The match with Hide-kun worked well by facing the pressure and being honest.

00:03:53.010 --> 00:03:57.290
Then, if I spit out my anger honestly, there is a possibility that I can change my power.

00:04:01.530 --> 00:04:07.220
I'm leading by two points, so I'm going to go all-out and use the anger I've endured so far as a counterattack!

00:04:07.420 --> 00:04:07.940
Kyaa!

00:04:08.020 --> 00:04:09.070
Bukkuru!

00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:09.450
Ugh!

00:04:12.090 --> 00:04:12.470
Ah!

00:04:12.510 --> 00:04:13.390
Awa Maruo!

00:04:13.490 --> 00:04:16.920
Is he okay?

00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:19.390
He must have been upset because of what happened earlier.

00:04:19.730 --> 00:04:22.770
Even the big brother of the Onkou is getting on my nerves.

00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:25.810
The 9th place is good, but the direction is bad.

00:04:26.440 --> 00:04:28.220
But if I fix it, I can do it.

00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:29.980
I don't know what to do.

00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:33.430
If you can spit out your anger, I'll release your anger!

00:04:34.810 --> 00:04:43.230
The swing is too fast, so it's a frame shot!

00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:46.330
But the swing itself has power.

00:04:46.770 --> 00:04:48.680
If you can get the timing right,

00:04:49.060 --> 00:04:52.800
Is it too much of a pin?

00:04:54.230 --> 00:04:55.840
Match the faster swing.

00:04:55.840 --> 00:04:56.480
The timing is perfect!

00:05:04.990 --> 00:05:08.150
I can't match the timing at all even though I'm going in from the beginning.

00:05:08.150 --> 00:05:11.160
I hope I can win, but I can't keep the odds.

00:05:11.820 --> 00:05:13.140
No good.

00:05:13.320 --> 00:05:15.370
I can't let Hikari go to the match.

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:18.320
Two and a half years of career.

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:19.180
I'm inexperienced.

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:23.100
My heart rate is going up.

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:25.520
My head is not as clear as usual.

00:05:25.900 --> 00:05:28.660
I didn't think it would really affect me.

00:05:31.820 --> 00:05:33.820
We need to take some time here.

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:37.140
I'm sorry!

00:05:37.420 --> 00:05:39.420
Please take a time violation.

00:05:41.228 --> 00:05:42.368
15 seconds.

00:05:42.476 --> 00:05:42.976
Eh?

00:05:42.976 --> 00:05:44.096
Mario-senshu...

00:05:44.236 --> 00:05:48.136
The points are a little longer than before, so please be careful.

00:05:48.460 --> 00:05:48.960
Yes, ma'am!

00:05:49.164 --> 00:05:50.164
I-I'm sorry!

00:05:50.924 --> 00:05:51.424
and so on.

00:05:51.724 --> 00:05:54.964
If the point is more than 20 seconds, you will receive a warning.

00:05:55.084 --> 00:05:58.524
He really is a nasty person.

00:06:00.730 --> 00:06:08.320
No, no, if I get angry, it's the opposite effect. I have to change my mind once. I have to purify my anger somehow.

00:06:08.460 --> 00:06:13.380
That's right. Takagi-kun is just doing it within the scope of the rules.

00:06:13.980 --> 00:06:17.370
That means I just couldn't think of a way to win Takagi-kun.

00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:27.350
If I was the one who hit the ball that aimed at the front, I was the one who couldn't take care of it.

00:06:27.350 --> 00:06:29.310
I'll be careful not to get my feet wet.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:35.540
It's my lack of experience, so it's a fair tactic to go under serve.

00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:41.130
Fifteen seconds.

00:06:42.160 --> 00:06:43.480
Five more seconds and I'll warn you.

00:06:44.540 --> 00:06:48.090
But the time-break five-all is the most important point.

00:06:48.210 --> 00:06:51.010
The ball grabs the set point.

00:06:51.610 --> 00:06:52.820
You can't drop it no matter what.

00:06:53.800 --> 00:06:57.720
Maruo, 20 seconds have passed.

00:06:57.940 --> 00:06:58.400
Warning.

00:07:00.760 --> 00:07:02.220
Hey, Maruo received a warning.

00:07:02.740 --> 00:07:07.070
If you receive a warning again in 20 seconds, you'll lose points.

00:07:07.370 --> 00:07:09.750
What are you doing, bro?

00:07:10.190 --> 00:07:17.530
I'll accept the warning.

00:07:18.430 --> 00:07:22.040
But for now, I'll take this place for sure.

00:07:22.140 --> 00:07:26.070
For that, I'll use the remaining 20 seconds to stabilize my confused feelings.

00:07:27.510 --> 00:07:29.650
I dare to receive a warning.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:34.820
I'm the same as Takagi-kun. I'm not in a position to talk about other people.

00:07:37.240 --> 00:07:39.260
It's the rule to decide who's the best in the court.

00:07:40.100 --> 00:07:42.980
Takagi-kun is Takagi-kun's way of doing things.

00:07:43.140 --> 00:07:47.790
I just have to fight like myself.

00:08:04.320 --> 00:08:05.500
I'm not angry anymore!

00:08:05.560 --> 00:08:09.810
What's with that face?

00:08:10.030 --> 00:08:13.240
If you can do it, then try it!

00:08:13.480 --> 00:08:19.520
Even if I'm angry, nothing will get better.

00:08:19.760 --> 00:08:22.770
I believe that my body understands that too.

00:08:27.050 --> 00:08:28.140
Savistas!

00:08:30.320 --> 00:08:30.640
Frame!

00:08:33.690 --> 00:08:34.890
6-5, Maruo.

00:08:35.030 --> 00:08:36.340
That was close.

00:08:36.880 --> 00:08:41.450
But even though his body was stiff, he was able to score points without fear.

00:08:42.310 --> 00:08:48.140
If you think about it calmly, Takagi-kun's fear is not inferior to his bad manners.

00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:50.840
His movements are not inferior to his bad manners.

00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:52.790
His stamina is the threat.

00:08:53.130 --> 00:08:58.120
If he drops the first set, he will have to fight with that stamina in the full set.

00:09:01.150 --> 00:09:04.820
I didn't realize it until now. I really lost sight of something important.

00:09:05.830 --> 00:09:11.300
When my anger subsided, I felt a kind of pressure.

00:09:12.020 --> 00:09:18.510
But if I can control this kind of pressure, I'll become a weapon.

00:09:18.970 --> 00:09:23.480
It's a set point. I'll decide it here.

00:09:23.560 --> 00:09:25.790
Don't endure more than you think.

00:09:25.930 --> 00:09:29.830
But if you do this far, the rest is going to be fine and at once.

00:09:30.350 --> 00:09:33.220
I don't know where Nabae is agreeing with this guy.

00:09:33.860 --> 00:09:35.100
I don't agree!

00:09:39.730 --> 00:09:41.390
After a strong flat and a return,

00:09:41.810 --> 00:09:43.770
with a shot that hasn't been hit so far...

00:09:43.770 --> 00:09:44.900
It's a draw!

00:09:44.960 --> 00:09:46.320
A drop!

00:09:55.450 --> 00:09:57.470
Count 7-6

00:09:57.470 --> 00:09:58.640
All right!

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:03.750
That was a good serve, but why?

00:10:04.680 --> 00:10:12.540
If he calms down, he might be able to feel the pressure.

00:10:15.860 --> 00:10:17.540
It was a match with Ida-kun who was heavily caught up in it.

00:10:18.600 --> 00:10:20.280
This feeling...

00:10:20.280 --> 00:10:22.260
I can do this!

00:10:22.300 --> 00:10:29.730
From the second set...

00:10:30.410 --> 00:10:33.870
I'll take more risks and raise my gear one step higher!

00:10:35.560 --> 00:10:38.120
If I stand in the lead with a quick serve from Kludd,

00:10:38.440 --> 00:10:40.210
I'll make a loose, deep spin!

00:10:40.390 --> 00:10:44.500
I'll attack with an unexpected slice and a precise attack!

00:10:50.160 --> 00:10:52.180
What was that?

00:10:52.540 --> 00:10:54.130
Isn't that a painful play?

00:10:54.770 --> 00:10:56.670
This is good enough!

00:10:56.670 --> 00:10:59.740
Takagi, who I easily lost to...

00:11:00.990 --> 00:11:02.070
Aniki has gotten stronger.

00:11:02.610 --> 00:11:08.730
Such a flashy play, in Aniki's case, is a matter of practice.

00:11:09.610 --> 00:11:10.670
Dash 10 times!

00:11:11.050 --> 00:11:14.460
Aniki is practicing all the techniques in a balanced way.

00:11:14.840 --> 00:11:17.370
That's why he can do a lot of things.

00:11:19.480 --> 00:11:20.760
Alright, that was good.

00:11:21.340 --> 00:11:24.040
With that attitude, 10 more!

00:11:24.200 --> 00:11:25.380
Next is the backhand!

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:28.600
Come to think of it...

00:11:30.030 --> 00:11:31.610
Maruo, have you ever done a shoulder-pull shot?

00:11:33.250 --> 00:11:34.740
Is that something like a song?

00:11:36.630 --> 00:11:38.600
No, that's a proper shot.

00:11:39.840 --> 00:11:43.930
You're pulled over by a rope, but you're barely able to catch up.

00:11:44.110 --> 00:11:45.490
But you don't have the time to look back and shoot.

00:11:46.810 --> 00:11:51.030
In that case, it's better to pull out your shoulder rather than looking back.

00:11:51.790 --> 00:11:53.430
And it's harder to read the course.

00:11:53.590 --> 00:11:53.990
Yes!

00:11:55.840 --> 00:11:56.900
You should be this fast.

00:11:57.980 --> 00:11:59.760
You're good.

00:12:00.090 --> 00:12:02.480
I heard he's a former professional.

00:12:03.260 --> 00:12:04.430
Here you go, Maruo!

00:12:04.650 --> 00:12:04.710
Oh!

00:12:04.870 --> 00:12:05.310
Ah!

00:12:05.840 --> 00:12:06.320
Ah!

00:12:07.080 --> 00:12:07.100
Ow!

00:12:07.160 --> 00:12:07.920
That was scary!

00:12:08.740 --> 00:12:09.940
Bring the ball to the end of the second round.

00:12:12.280 --> 00:12:12.760
Ah!

00:12:14.540 --> 00:12:14.860
That was close!

00:12:15.380 --> 00:12:15.800
You!

00:12:16.740 --> 00:12:21.320
Good job, Maruo!

00:12:21.600 --> 00:12:21.900
Yes!

00:12:23.320 --> 00:12:25.540
My brother's growth is the result of his practice.

00:12:26.460 --> 00:12:29.820
Game Maruo 1-0 Second Set

00:12:30.220 --> 00:12:31.570
Okay, keep it.

00:12:31.830 --> 00:12:32.860
I'm getting used to it.

00:12:35.400 --> 00:12:39.100
I'm getting used to it.

00:12:39.180 --> 00:12:39.460
I'm getting used to it.

00:12:39.760 --> 00:12:40.830
I'm getting used to it.

00:12:41.530 --> 00:12:42.010
I'm getting used to it.

00:12:42.010 --> 00:12:42.750
I'm getting used to it.

00:12:42.830 --> 00:12:47.740
I can't see Takagi's weak point, but I can't see his strength like Ide-kun and Araya-kun.

00:12:48.560 --> 00:12:51.850
If I can play my tennis, I won't lose.

00:12:52.090 --> 00:12:55.600
But I don't know what I'm going to do, so I'm just going to be careful.

00:12:55.600 --> 00:12:56.640
It's not worth it to be in this world.

00:13:00.670 --> 00:13:06.610
I-I can't believe it!

00:13:07.050 --> 00:13:11.500
I can't afford to lose before I fight Nabae!

00:13:11.500 --> 00:13:12.340
What?

00:13:14.250 --> 00:13:25.720
The referee's condition is getting worse.

00:13:25.940 --> 00:13:29.980
I was on the line, but the referee's judgment...

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:34.320
Game Maruo 2-0 Second Set

00:13:35.920 --> 00:13:49.630
Break the head of the second set

00:13:50.190 --> 00:13:52.260
And one more

00:13:52.260 --> 00:13:53.100
Raise the gear!

00:14:04.370 --> 00:14:11.550
I don't know what and how I analyzed it, but I can handle it in a blink of an eye!

00:14:14.840 --> 00:14:19.900
What's next to a fast flat? Sliding? Bouncing? Is that fast? Slow?

00:14:20.280 --> 00:14:24.740
No, it's a continuous high-speed flat!

00:14:25.260 --> 00:14:27.700
Game Maruo 3-0 Second Set

00:14:27.700 --> 00:14:28.220
Alright!

00:14:36.650 --> 00:14:39.950
If you rely only on your small hands, your tennis will really not grow.

00:14:41.420 --> 00:14:42.640
Nabae is right.

00:14:43.060 --> 00:14:49.050
Game Maruo 4-1 Second Set

00:14:49.050 --> 00:14:52.890
I already know. This guy is...

00:14:53.260 --> 00:14:56.780
Game Maruo 5-2 Second Set

00:14:56.780 --> 00:14:57.690
I can't win with my small hands.

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:01.210
Big brother is waiting for you!

00:15:01.670 --> 00:15:05.540
Game Set and Match 1 by Maruo

00:15:05.540 --> 00:15:08.320
Count 7, 6, 6, 2

00:15:08.320 --> 00:15:13.100
Thank you very much!

00:15:13.340 --> 00:15:24.500
I practiced more than Navai

00:15:24.500 --> 00:15:27.970
Certainly, the time was saved for the shot and strategy at the tip of the stick

00:15:27.970 --> 00:15:29.520
I will lower the basic practice

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:30.620
I didn't do anything stupid.

00:15:30.740 --> 00:15:33.230
What should I do now?

00:15:34.580 --> 00:15:35.860
Maruo won again.

00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:38.280
No seed is the best four?

00:15:38.650 --> 00:15:42.190
Really? He started tennis in high school, right?

00:15:42.620 --> 00:15:45.800
That means it's only been two years.

00:15:46.220 --> 00:15:47.720
Brother, congratulations.

00:15:49.070 --> 00:15:50.090
Thank you.

00:15:50.230 --> 00:15:51.580
As expected of my brother.

00:15:52.310 --> 00:15:53.430
You did a good job.

00:15:53.970 --> 00:15:54.530
Yes.

00:15:55.660 --> 00:15:58.310
It would have been dangerous if I had taken the first set.

00:15:58.490 --> 00:15:59.050
Yes.

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:05.250
There are some players who are like that, but if you worry about it and struggle, you can't go up.

00:16:06.040 --> 00:16:09.000
Especially if you're planning to go overseas.

00:16:10.200 --> 00:16:16.230
Well, there's nothing to say about being irritated during the game.

00:16:17.010 --> 00:16:19.730
Yes, I understand that very well.

00:16:20.170 --> 00:16:25.270
The timing doesn't match and I'm tired, and I didn't even notice that I was under pressure.

00:16:26.950 --> 00:16:29.420
Pressure means you want to win.

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:34.030
It comes from your feelings, but anger comes from something that has nothing to do with it.

00:16:35.030 --> 00:16:47.620
My heartbeat...

00:16:47.620 --> 00:16:49.790
That's why it's better when you're under pressure.

00:16:51.350 --> 00:16:57.360
That's right. It's pretty surprising, isn't it?

00:16:57.360 --> 00:16:59.260
You're in a good mental state.

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:01.860
It looks like this when you put it in order.

00:17:01.920 --> 00:17:03.740
If you remember, Izu,

00:17:04.340 --> 00:17:07.860
what kind of mental state you are in right now

00:17:07.860 --> 00:17:09.720
and what direction you should go.

00:17:10.420 --> 00:17:16.870
You had a good experience, didn't you?

00:17:17.010 --> 00:17:20.190
Hey, can I ask you something?

00:17:20.290 --> 00:17:22.230
Takagi-kun?

00:17:22.790 --> 00:17:25.320
Is it true that you started tennis in high school?

00:17:26.460 --> 00:17:26.800
What?

00:17:30.030 --> 00:17:31.330
Yes, that's right.

00:17:32.280 --> 00:17:34.040
What is it all of a sudden?

00:17:34.520 --> 00:17:38.390
If you don't mind, can you tell me what kind of training you usually do?

00:17:40.460 --> 00:17:45.030
But...

00:17:46.010 --> 00:17:50.050
Is that the notebook you were using during the match?

00:17:50.470 --> 00:17:51.850
Oh, yes.

00:17:52.190 --> 00:17:54.190
Let me see it for a moment.

00:18:01.470 --> 00:18:04.140
Amazing! Most of the points are written!

00:18:04.520 --> 00:18:06.490
I'll just say it for the time being,

00:18:06.750 --> 00:18:10.730
even if you imitate what this guy is doing as it is, you won't be able to become strong.

00:18:11.350 --> 00:18:16.540
And you and this guy have different personalities and personalities.

00:18:17.740 --> 00:18:23.900
Maruo is practicing to be able to know himself and to be able to meet himself.

00:18:24.840 --> 00:18:29.560
He's using his precious personality and his lack of physical ability.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:33.550
By doing so, I'm trying to find my own tennis.

00:18:34.630 --> 00:18:36.960
My own tennis?

00:18:37.370 --> 00:18:39.740
I decided on the menu with Nabae.

00:18:41.480 --> 00:18:46.200
It may be unnecessary, but I think you have practice for yourself.

00:18:46.980 --> 00:18:51.480
Today, from my point of view, I think it would have been more painful to make use of that blessed amount of exercise.

00:18:53.760 --> 00:18:55.200
Uh, yes.

00:18:57.550 --> 00:18:58.690
Thank you for this.

00:18:58.710 --> 00:18:59.110
Yeah.

00:19:00.060 --> 00:19:03.320
No, um, can I ask you something?

00:19:03.760 --> 00:19:05.250
Oh, yeah.

00:19:05.450 --> 00:19:08.450
I heard that Takagi-kun has won against Nabae-kun before.

00:19:09.830 --> 00:19:10.960
How did you win?

00:19:13.010 --> 00:19:14.510
Where did you hear that from?

00:19:14.570 --> 00:19:17.020
I can't say I won against him.

00:19:17.720 --> 00:19:22.810
I only won once after playing a one-on-one match for more than 9 hours until I won.

00:19:23.610 --> 00:19:26.330
But I wanted to win once in the official match.

00:19:27.370 --> 00:19:29.330
You want to play until you win?

00:19:30.440 --> 00:19:34.470
He's an amazing person. He only gave me one set.

00:19:35.330 --> 00:19:36.210
What about you, Nabai-kun?

00:19:36.470 --> 00:19:43.770
It was kind of bad during the match, wasn't it?

00:19:44.100 --> 00:19:45.710
No, it was good for both of us.

00:19:46.010 --> 00:19:52.600
Well then, since you beat me, why don't you beat Nabai?

00:19:53.900 --> 00:19:55.200
Who do you want me to beat?

00:19:55.520 --> 00:19:58.050
Oh, Nabai-kun.

00:19:58.170 --> 00:19:59.980
That means...

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:01.960
Maruo-kun won, didn't he?

00:20:01.960 --> 00:20:02.280
Yeah.

00:20:03.460 --> 00:20:05.730
Well then, I'll be in your care tomorrow.

00:20:06.590 --> 00:20:07.690
I'll be in your care, too.

00:20:08.990 --> 00:20:10.550
Nabai-kun won, too.

00:20:10.630 --> 00:20:20.270
Next is the number one in the All Japan Junior Ranking,

00:20:21.810 --> 00:20:22.530
Nabai-kun!

00:20:22.610 --> 00:20:25.730
He was strong, wasn't he, Maruo-kun?

00:20:26.420 --> 00:20:29.640
Well, he's been playing tennis for two and a half years.

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:32.020
Eh? I didn't know that.

00:20:32.200 --> 00:20:33.900
You didn't know?

00:20:34.240 --> 00:20:35.990
I thought you were growing fast.

00:20:37.750 --> 00:20:41.430
If I think about it, my efforts are a lot of waste.

00:20:41.870 --> 00:20:44.700
Efforts don't have to be wasted.

00:20:45.380 --> 00:20:45.560
Huh?

00:20:46.670 --> 00:20:51.420
Just because you didn't live today, your efforts will definitely live someday.

00:20:51.560 --> 00:20:55.400
But anyway, I'm going to stop relying on my hands.

00:20:56.460 --> 00:20:59.580
Eh? Are you going to stop that?

00:21:00.670 --> 00:21:02.690
You told me to stop!

00:21:03.770 --> 00:21:05.600
Well, that's true.

00:21:05.880 --> 00:21:08.460
But if I can do it well, I can be a good weapon.

00:21:09.000 --> 00:21:11.290
I also want to wear it somewhere.

00:21:12.050 --> 00:21:14.240
Then which one?

00:21:15.410 --> 00:21:15.710
That's not good.

00:21:15.910 --> 00:21:18.790
That's not good enough.

00:21:20.090 --> 00:21:23.690
But you're not losing to anyone in your own way.

00:21:24.950 --> 00:21:27.790
So I'm sure you're going to come back sooner or later.

00:21:31.690 --> 00:21:34.330
W-What's wrong with you? You're making me feel bad.

00:21:34.690 --> 00:21:36.970
What's wrong with you? You're praising me.

00:21:37.230 --> 00:21:41.620
Oh, by the way, I have something to ask you.

00:21:42.970 --> 00:21:43.530
You...

00:21:45.000 --> 00:21:45.540
He's really scary.

00:21:46.160 --> 00:21:51.320
Big brother, this is finally the best 4.

00:21:51.640 --> 00:21:52.740
Y-Yeah.

00:21:53.110 --> 00:21:57.200
We won against that Takagi, and Big brother's abilities are already real.

00:21:57.640 --> 00:21:59.900
Nabae-sen.

00:22:01.308 --> 00:22:03.308
I'm looking forward to it.

00:22:05.404 --> 00:22:07.404
Thank you for watching.

00:22:15.644 --> 00:22:17.044
I lost last year.

00:22:17.820 --> 00:22:20.220
I'll do my best from now on.

00:22:20.732 --> 00:22:22.012
I'm finally here.

00:24:00.636 --> 00:24:01.396
Takuma-san!

00:24:01.436 --> 00:24:01.936
I...

00:24:02.108 --> 00:24:03.548
I'm in the top 4!

00:24:03.580 --> 00:24:05.620
So, you're going to Nabai tomorrow?

00:24:05.692 --> 00:24:06.692
What a pain in the ass.

00:24:06.716 --> 00:24:07.676
What about you, Nabai-kun?

00:24:07.680 --> 00:24:10.520
There are no physical or mental holes.

00:24:11.004 --> 00:24:12.404
I don't have the strength to fight.

00:24:12.404 --> 00:24:13.084
I see.

00:24:13.340 --> 00:24:14.560
Don't you know?

00:24:15.292 --> 00:24:16.772
When I was a kid, he was...

00:24:16.828 --> 00:24:18.828
There was a huge hole.

00:24:18.828 --> 00:24:19.588
What?

00:24:19.612 --> 00:24:20.692
...Nabai-kun?

00:24:21.244 --> 00:24:22.804
The next Baby Step is...

00:24:23.068 --> 00:24:24.668
Existence is the driving force!
